    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNew to the market is no 36 The Anchorage, a much sought after, stylish, modern development of apartments situated on the seafront in the heart of Dun Laoghaire. The complex is architecturally finished with a wonderful roof top terrace, landscaped communal gardens and full caretaker service. This second-floor apartment combines contemporary comfort with elegant interiors; this exceptional home offers a peaceful retreat just moments from the vibrant heart of the town.\nFlooded with natural light, the spacious open-plan living and dining area is thoughtfully designed for both relaxation and entertaining. A stunning feature fireplace creates a warm focal point, while large patio doors frame leafy views and open onto a private balcony, perfect for enjoying morning coffee or evening unwinding.\nThe stylish living space is finished to a high standard, featuring tasteful neutral décor, quality wooden flooring, and sophisticated furnishings that create an inviting and modern atmosphere. The adjoining dining area enjoys a bright outlook, ideal for everyday living or hosting guests.\nThe apartment benefits from a generously proportioned bedroom, a well-appointed contemporary bathroom, and a fully fitted kitchen designed for practical modern living.\nSituated within a secure and well-maintained development, The Anchorage offers residents a superb balance of tranquillity and convenience. Dún Laoghaire's renowned seafront, marina, boutique cafés, restaurants, shopping, and excellent transport links, including the DART which are all within easy reach.\n\nA winning combination, this fine property offers the discerning purchaser a truly impressive residence and must be viewed to be truly appreciated."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance hall: - 1.68m x 2.00m\ntiled flooring, central light, intercom, hot press\n\nLiving/dining room: - 6.43m x 4.10m\nwood flooring, central light, fireplace with wooden mantle and black stone hearth, gas fire insert, sliding patio doors to balcony\n\nKitchen: - 1.79m x 2.33m\nfloor and eyelevel cabinets, integrated electric oven and hob, extractor fan, plumbed for washing machine, under counter fridge, central light, stainless steel one and a half sink unit, tiled splashback, tiled floor.\n\nBedroom 1: - 6.43m x 2.75m\nwood flooring, double room, built in wardrobes, central light\n\nBathroom: - 2.25m x 1.71m\ntiled floors and walls, WC, wash handbasin, bath suite with telephone shower attachment\n\n"
      },
